1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:22,000
The Companion answers a bearing question using the selected business context and cited records.

2
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:39,000
A follow-up about its PMI retains the bearing context and returns the recorded dimensional limits.

3
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The saved question, answer and resolved context can be inspected after the conversation.

4
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Conversation records are retained in PostgreSQL while engineering knowledge remains in the published graph.

5
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Change Control retains publication decisions and their execution status for review.

6
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:48,000
The retained receipt identifies the execution actor and outcome without inventing an approval.

7
00:01:48,000 --> 00:02:04,000
The shaft record preserves revision B, its material and a 40 mm nominal diameter.

8
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Expanding the shaft reveals its previous revision, requirement, PMI, inspection and manufacturing links.

9
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:38,000
The quality record retains a measured 40.006 mm diameter and its pending engineering sign-off.

10
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:58,000
The Governor prepares a retained merge proposal from the selected Teamcenter and QIF vocabularies.

11
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Reviewers compare definitions and property context because a high lexical score does not establish equivalence.

12
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:32,000
The retained validation evidence blocks publication until the imported vocabulary defects are resolved.

13
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:48,000
The bearing requirement records a 25 mm bore and the evidence needed for verification.

14
00:03:48,000 --> 00:04:04,000
The MBSE block identifies the bearing subsystem separately from its managed product records.

15
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Expanding the subsystem exposes its recorded assembly allocation and requirement relationship.

16
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:36,000
The inner race retains its part number, revision A and 25 mm bore diameter.

17
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:54,000
The manufacturing BOM connects component identities and individual BOM lines for traceability review.

18
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:10,000
The linked CAD reference retains its document identity and the brg_2001_A.jt file name.

19
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:26,000
The cylindrical bore is represented separately from the part with its 25 mm nominal dimension.

20
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:42,000
The bore PMI records datum A and dimensional limits from 24.99 to 25.01 mm.

21
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:58,000
The inspection records a measured 25.006 mm bore within the stated dimensional limits.

22
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Expanding the inspection returns to the inspected part and its verification requirement.

23
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Recorded relationships connect requirements, parts, CAD, PMI, manufacturing and quality for engineering review.
